/*
 * ESP32-C5-WROOM-1 interim dev-bench board (embarch-dev-bench/design.md's
 * ESP JTAG interim decision). Auto-merged by Zephyr's board devicetree
 * overlay convention (flat filename matching the board target, same as this
 * board's own .conf fragment) -- no extra CMake wiring needed.
 *
 * Second real end-to-end finding on this exact link, Milestone 3 (Study
 * Designer: Feature-Branch Iteration), 2026-08-20 -- this file previously
 * repointed the console/protocol link at `usb_serial` (the native USB
 * JTAG/serial peripheral, same physical USB-C port used for JTAG flashing),
 * because `uart0`'s header pins were believed disconnected from anything
 * the host could reach. That's wrong for this specific board: the
 * ESP32-C5-DevKitC-1 has a *second* USB-C port, wired to `uart0` through its
 * own onboard USB-UART bridge chip, entirely separate from the native USB
 * JTAG/serial port both live in the same DTS as `zephyr,console = &uart0`
 * (the board's own upstream default) already assumed. Found live: the first
 * real `run_study` against `usb_serial` got past Core's dev-bench port
 * *detection* (unambiguous once `EMBARCH_DEV_BENCH_SERIAL` was set) but
 * failed decoding `HelloAck` -- consistent with the native USB JTAG/serial
 * peripheral's poll-mode driver not reliably carrying this link's 1 Mbaud
 * binary protocol, not a framing/logic bug (`CONFIG_LOG=n`, no stray
 * `printk` on this path -- checked, not assumed). Switching back to the
 * board's own default console (`uart0`, over its dedicated UART USB-C port)
 * tests that theory with zero rewiring: both USB-C ports stay connected,
 * JTAG flashing/reset keep using the native one, the protocol link moves to
 * the UART one. `current-speed` overridden to 1 Mbaud here (the upstream
 * default of 115200 predates this link needing to match
 * `embarch-core::dev_bench_link::DEV_BENCH_BAUD`). `usb_serial` is left
 * enabled -- harmless if unused, and JTAG/flashing over that same physical
 * port is unaffected by what Zephyr's console is chosen to.
 */

&uart0 {
	current-speed = <1000000>;
};
